cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its experimental data, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Kunlunxin-FFT: A Triton-Mapped FFT Operator Library for Kunlunxin P800"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Teng"
    family-names: "Wang"
    email: "wangt635@ustc.edu.cn"
    affiliation: "High Efficient Intelligent Computing Lab, Suzhou Institute for Advanced Research, University of Science and Technology of China, Suzhou, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TruNcat3/kunlunxin-fft"
url: "https://github.com/TruNcat3/kunlunxin-fft"
abstract: >-
  A Triton-mapped FFT operator library and reproducible research artifact for
  the Kunlunxin P800. It documents the executable device-code path
  (Triton -> XMLIR -> XPU instructions), records the dead ends that rule out
  nvcc/PTX, clang-written device code, and bare C++ ELF launching, and ships a
  correctness-verified radix-2 DIT/DIF complex FFT with a measured baseline
  against the vendor torch.fft.fft. The current implementation validates fp32
  C2C forward transforms for power-of-two lengths up to 1048576 on P800 while
  retaining an extensible design space for additional transforms and dataflow
  optimizations.
keywords:
  - FFT
  - Kunlunxin
  - P800
  - Triton
  - XMLIR
  - XPU
  - butterfly
  - signal-processing
license: Apache-2.0
